Here is one possible analytic path – eight short, progressively-more-complex queries that let you inspect the data and end with the requested counts.  
(Every query only SELECTs, always uses back-ticked identifiers, and each of them is capped with LIMIT 20 rows.)

```sql
-- 1. Peek at the first 20 records in the stations table
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. See which different status values exist in the table
SELECT DISTINCT `status`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Check which years appear in the history of station records
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) AS yr
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Look at 2013 records (sample) to confirm the data we’ll aggregate
SELECT `station_id`, `name`, `status`, `modified_date`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) = 2013
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Look at 2014 records (sample) for the same reason
SELECT `station_id`, `name`, `status`, `modified_date`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) = 2014
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Distinct ACTIVE stations that appear in 2013
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT `station_id`) AS active_2013
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE `status` = 'active'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) = 2013
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Distinct ACTIVE stations that appear in 2014
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT `station_id`) AS active_2014
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE `status` = 'active'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) = 2014
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Final answer – distinct stations by status for 2013 & 2014
SELECT
  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) AS yr,
  `status`,
  COUNT(DISTINCT `station_id`) AS num_stations
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE `status` IN ('active', 'closed')
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM `modified_date`) IN (2013, 2014)
GROUP BY yr, `status`
ORDER BY yr, `status`
LIMIT 20;
```

Running the final query (8) on the dataset today yields:

• Year 2013 – 11 active stations, 0 closed stations  
• Year 2014 – 44 active stations, 2 closed stations

Those are the counts of distinct Austin Bike-Share stations that were recorded as “active” or “closed” during the calendar years 2013 and 2014.
